# Evidence bytes are HASH-REGISTERED. Git must never rewrite them.
#
# Found 2026-08-01, immediately after `evidence/` was created (ADR 0038). The commit output said:
#
#   warning: LF will be replaced by CRLF in evidence/phase6-sweep/points.json
#
# This machine has `core.autocrlf=true`. The committed blob is correct — it is LF and its sha256 is
# the registered `0ed613bc…` — but autocrlf converts on CHECKOUT, so a fresh clone on Windows would
# write CRLF into the working tree and **every sha256 printed in the published reports would fail
# against the file the reader actually has.** The evidence would be intact in the object store and
# unverifiable in practice, which is the worst of both.
#
# `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion in both directions while keeping the files diffable
# (unlike `binary`, which would also suppress diffs on what are JSON and SVG).
#
# The rule is deliberately the whole subtree: an evidence file added later must not have to remember
# this.
evidence/** -text

# The manifests are the checking mechanism for the above, so they get the same treatment.
evidence/MANIFEST.json -text
evidence/OUT-TREES-MANIFEST.json -text

# This archive deliberately preserves a mixed-CRLF/LF historical buffer byte-for-byte. Without an
# exact-path override, this Windows host's core.autocrlf=true clean filter changes it while adding
# the file, so the committed blob would not match the recorded raw-body identity. Git's whitespace
# checker otherwise treats each preserved CR byte as trailing whitespace, so disable that one check
# only for this exact immutable archive path.
docs/progress-history-through-2026-08-02.md -text whitespace=-trailing-space

# The live source audit and exact rejected V4/V4.x history must survive Windows checkout byte-exact.
research/phase6-source-currency.md -text
research/rejected/phase6-wp1-v4x/phase6-source-currency-v4x-rejected.md -text
research/rejected/phase6-wp1-v4x/phase6-wp1-independence-operands.json -text
research/rejected/phase6-wp1-v4x/phase6-wp1-review-findings.json -text
research/rejected/phase6-wp1-v4x/phase6-wp1-search-registry.json -text
